BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monkey Business in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260902T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260902T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc88b-243a-ad10-b3bf-fcbe2f99ee0d@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, September 2\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy
  Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 37m\n\n1952 | 97 min | USA | Bla
 ck-and-White | English | Not Rated | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Howard Hawks \n
 PRODUCED BY: Sol C. Siegel \nWRITTEN BY: Ben Hecht\, Charles Lederer\, I. 
 A. L. Diamond \nWITH: Cary Grant\, Ginger Rogers\, Charles Coburn\, Marily
 n Monroe\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDr. Barnaby Fulton (Cary Grant) is a scatt
 erbrained chemist working to create an elixir of youth. When one of his ch
 impanzees\, Esther\, breaks loose\, she mixes chemicals in Barnaby’s lab
 \, dumping the concoction into the office’s water cooler. The formula ge
 nerates the rejuvenation effect Barnaby has been seeking — along with mo
 re chaotic side effects in some cases. Monkey Business allowed Monroe\, wh
 o co-stars as Lois Laurel\, to showcase her brilliant timing\, further sol
 idifying her reputation as a comedic actress.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/monkey-business-019fc
 88b-243a-ad10-b3bf-fcbe2f99ee0d
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Women
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260902T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260902T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc8a7-c694-982e-f68b-8d69273eeb1d@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Academy Governor Patricia Dehaney \nSelected by the
  Makeup Artists and Hairstylists Branch\n\nWednesday\, September 2\, 2026 
 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 1
 3m\n\n1939 | 133 min. | USA | Black-and-white\, color | English | DCP \nD
 IRECTED BY: George Cukor \nPRODUCED BY: Hunt Stromberg \nWRITTEN BY: Anit
 a Loos\, Jane Murfin \nWITH: Norma Shearer\, Joan Crawford\, Rosalind Russ
 ell\, Mary Boland\n\nType: Screenings\n\nCo-written by Anita Loos and Jane
  Murfin\, The Women delivers 135 of them\, each with a speaking role\, to 
 the exclusion of men. The delightfully witty and rapid-fire dialogue pours
  out of a cadre of familiar faces\, including Norma Shearer\, Joan Crawfor
 d\, and Rosalind Russell. While most of the film unfolds in black-and-whit
 e\, a delightful six-minute Technicolor fashion show is included\, featuri
 ng gowns by Adrian\, the iconic\, MGM-based costume designer. Contributing
  to the distinctive looks of the cast was the uncredited hair designer\, M
 GM veteran Sydney Guilaroff\, whose film career spanned the 1930s to the 1
 980s and included such classics as Singin’ in the Rain (1952)\, North by
  Northwest (1959) and Who’s Afraid of Virginia Woolf? (1966)
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-women-019fc8a7-c6
 94-982e-f68b-8d69273eeb1d
END:VEVENT
