BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Barry Lyndon in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc89b-1225-eeaf-4075-7229824fea60@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, September 3\, 2026 at 7 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 3h 5m\n\n1975 | 185 min | UK\, USA | Co
 lor | English | Rated PG | 35mm  \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN/PRODUCED BY: Stanley 
 Kubrick.  \nWITH: Ryan O’Neal\, Marisa Berenson\, Patrick Magee\, Hardy
  Kruger.  \nNew print courtesy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Scre
 enings\n\nStanley Kubrick’s follow-up to the foreboding A Clockwork Oran
 ge (1971) is a stately\, gorgeously crafted\, epic adaptation of William M
 akepeace Thackeray’s novel about the curious fates of an Irish rogue. Ry
 an O’Neal portrays Lyndon\, and the film earned seven nominations\, incl
 uding Best Picture\, Directing\, and Adapted Screenplay (all for Kubrick)
 \, with Oscars going to the Art Direction\, Costume Design\, Adaptation Sc
 ore\, and John Alcott’s painterly\, natural and candlelit cinematography
 \, which remains immensely influential.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/barry-lyndon-019fc89b
 -1225-eeaf-4075-7229824fea60
END:VEVENT
