BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Adventures of Priscilla\, Queen of the Desert in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260909T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260909T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc8a9-66fc-e4d3-eba1-d926c379596d@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Selected by the Marketing and Public Relations Branch\n\nWedne
 sday\, September 9\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion
  Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 44m\n\n1994 | 104 min. | Australia | Color | Scop
 e | English | Rated R | 35mm\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Stephan Elliott \nPRODU
 CED BY: Al Clark\, Michael Hamlyn \nWITH: Terence Stamp\, Hugo Weaving\, G
 uy Pearce\, Bill Hunter\nPrint courtesy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nTy
 pe: Screenings\n\nTwo drag queens and a transgender woman drive across the
  Australian outback in a tour bus named Priscilla\, in this wild road come
 dy that earned Lizzy Gardiner and Tim Chappell Oscars for their imaginativ
 e costume designs. Terence Stamp gives an impressive change-of-pace perfor
 mance as the world-weary Bernadette\, and he’s matched by Hugo Weaving a
 s the trio’s conflicted leader. Guy Pearce delivers a breakout performan
 ce as the youngest of the group. Deftly mixing campy humor and genuine emo
 tion amidst stunning locations\, Priscilla was an international success an
 d spawned a hit stage musical.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-adventures-of-pri
 scilla-queen-of-the-desert-019fc8a9-66fc-e4d3-eba1-d926c379596d
END:VEVENT
