BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Far from Heaven in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260923T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260923T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc8ab-593d-505e-89af-09d3a09dd244@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: producer Brad Simpson and Academy Governor Effie T.
  Brown \nSelected by the Producers Branch\n\nWednesday\, September 23\, 20
 26 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1
 h 47m\n\n2002 | 107 min. | USA | Color | English | Rated PG-13 | 35mm \nDI
 RECTED/WRITTEN BY: Todd Haynes \nPRODUCED BY: Christine Vachon\, Jody Patt
 on \nWITH: Julianne Moore\, Dennis Quaid\, Dennis Haysbert\, Patricia Clar
 kson \nPrint courtesy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\n
 A suburban housewife discovers her husband has a secret life\, only to fin
 d herself becoming emotionally involved with another man\, in writer-direc
 tor Todd Haynes’s sincere and expertly crafted homage to the 1950s melod
 ramas of Douglas Sirk. Best Actress nominee Julianne Moore gives a perfect
 ly pitched lead performance\, with strong support from Dennis Quaid\, Denn
 is Haysbert\, Patricia Clarkson and Viola Davis. The film also received no
 minations for Haynes’s sensitive screenplay\, Edward Lachman’s autumna
 l cinematography\, and the gorgeously old-fashioned score by Elmer Bernste
 in. One of the film’s producers is Haynes’s longtime collaborator Chri
 stine Vachon\, one of this year’s Governors Awards winners (with longtim
 e filmmaking partner Pamela Koffler) for her remarkable and groundbreaking
  career.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/far-from-heaven-019fc
 8ab-593d-505e-89af-09d3a09dd244
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gallery Spotlight: Dissident Cinema and Bong Joon Ho
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T130000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019ff303-33b4-2e43-7aaf-7ea259c6d2ad@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Conversations
DESCRIPTION:Author Karen Han appears at the Academy Museum to deliver rare
  insight on Oscar-winning director Bong Joon Ho.\n\nFriday\, September 25
 \, 2026 at 12 pm\n\nLocation: TMT Lobby\, Lower Level 1 (LL1)\n\nCost: Fre
 e with general admission\n\nType: Conversations\n\nAuthor Karen Han appear
 s at the Academy Museum to deliver rare insight on Oscar-winning director 
 Bong Joon Ho. She discusses the research behind her book Bong Joon Ho: Dis
 sident Cinema\, examining the career of the writer-director behind The Hos
 t (2006)\, Parasite (2019)\, Okja (2017) and other films that span a label
 -defying career. Dig deeper into the filmmaker’s work with the Academy M
 useum exhibition Director’s Inspiration: Bong Joon Ho. \nAbout Gallery S
 potlightsGallery Spotlights feature special guests who bring fresh insight
 s to our exhibitions. Join us for revealing monthly conversations connecti
 ng the objects in our galleries to the art and history of moviemaking.
LOCATION:TMT Lobby\, Lower Level 1 (LL1)
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/gallery-spotlight-dis
 sident-cinema-and-bong-joon-ho-019ff303-33b4-2e43-7aaf-7ea259c6d2ad
END:VEVENT
