BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Abbott and Costello Meet Frankenstein
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T121500
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc898-4964-4e59-8126-55aef8ca9d4b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Accessible Screening\n\nSaturday\, September 26\, 2026 at 11 a
 m\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 23m\n\n194
 8 | 83 min. | USA | Black-and-White | English | Open Captions | Recommende
 d for ages 7+ | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Charles T. Barton \nPRODUCED BY: Robe
 rt Arthur \nWRITTEN BY: Robert Lees\, Frederic I. Rinaldo\, John Grant 
 \nWITH: Bud Abbott\, Lou Costello\, Lon Chaney Jr.\, Bela Lugosi\n\nType: 
 Screenings\n\nAccessible screeningOn the last Saturday of every month\, th
 e museum's Family Matinee is an accessible screening where we offer open c
 aptioning\, keep the theater dimly lit\, and maintain a lower volume for v
 iewers who are neurodiverse. \nA popular comedy team of the 1940s and 1950
 s\, Bud Abbott and Lou Costello\, goes up against Universal Studios' monst
 ers in this zany spoof that inspired several creep-tastic sequels. After D
 racula (Bela Lugosi) teams with scientist Dr. Sandra Mornay (Lenore Aubert
 ) to hunt for a more sophisticated brain for Frankenstein’s Monster (Gle
 nn Strange)\, they settle on dim-witted but lovable Wilbur Grey\, played b
 y Costello. Thanks in part to memorable appearances by the Wolf Man (Lon C
 haney Jr.)\, and Vincent Price voicing the Invisible Man\, this horror com
 edy mashup manages to do justice to both horror and comedy genres―a feat
  frequently attempted but rarely achieved.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/abbott-and-costello-m
 eet-frankentstein-019fc898-4964-4e59-8126-55aef8ca9d4b
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Halloween with John Carpenter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc8bc-e468-3bc5-4967-67324b2f8ec4@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, September 26\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy
  Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 31m\n\n1978 | 91min | USA | Colo
 r | Scope | English | Rated R | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: John Carpenter \nPRODUC
 ED BY: Debra Hill \nWRITTEN BY: John Carpenter\, Debra Hill \nWITH: Donald
  Pleasence\, Jamie Lee Curtis\, Nancy Loomis\, P. J. Soles\n\nType: Screen
 ings\n\nOn Halloween night\, 1963\, in the small Illinois town of Haddonfi
 eld\, 6-year-old Michael Myers commits a horribly violent act against his 
 older sister. Fifteen years later\, he escapes from a mental institution\,
  returns to Haddonfield on Halloween\, and stalks teenage babysitter Lauri
 e Strode (Jamie Lee Curtis\, in her feature film debut) while psychiatrist
  Dr. Loomis (Donald Pleasence) tries to find him. Released in 1978\, Hallo
 ween is a pioneering slasher film that established Curtis as a scream quee
 n.  Driven by John Carpenter’s sharp direction and staging\, coupled wit
 h the use of POV shots and his now-iconic\, eerie piano score\, Halloween 
 went on to become one of the most profitable independent films of all time
 \, leading to numerous sequels\, reboots\, remakes and many other adaptati
 ons.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/halloween-with-john-c
 arpenter-019fc8bc-e468-3bc5-4967-67324b2f8ec4
END:VEVENT
