BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Doctor Zhivago
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc8b6-eb8f-e390-20b3-65c983b6d891@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, September 27\, 2026 at 2 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 3h 17m\n\n1965 | 197 min. | USA | Color 
 | Scope | English | Rated PG-13 | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: David Lean \nWRITTEN 
 BY: Robert Bolt \nPRODUCED BY: Carlo Ponti \nWITH: Geraldine Chaplin\, Jul
 ie Christie\, Tom Courtenay\, Omar Sharif\n\nType: Screenings\n\nJohn Box 
 and his Oscar-winning production design team (art director Terence Marsh a
 nd set decorator Dario Simoni) built early 20th century Moscow on elaborat
 e sets in Spain as well as created Zhivago’s unforgettable ice palace fo
 r this David Lean-directed romantic epic. The resulting adaptation of the 
 novel by Nobel Prize-winner Boris Pasternak became a box office smash. Oma
 r Sharif and Julie Christie lead the all-star cast\, with Maurice Jarre’
 s score (featuring “Lara’s Theme”) receiving one of the film’s fiv
 e Oscars\, which also included Color Cinematography (Freddie Young)\, Colo
 r Costume Design (Phyllis Dalton) and adapted screenplay (Robert Bolt).
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/doctor-zhivago-019fc8
 b6-eb8f-e390-20b3-65c983b6d891
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:They Live with John Carpenter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc8bd-7eb2-9037-e9c7-c5ede38fe138@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, September 27\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy M
 useum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 34m\n\n1988 | 94min | USA | Color 
 and Black-and-White | Scope | English | Rated R | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Jo
 hn Carpenter \nPRODUCED BY: Larry Franco \nWRITTEN BY: John Carpenter \nWI
 TH: Roddy Piper\, Keith David\, Meg Foster\, George "Buck" Flower\n\nType:
  Screenings\n\nWhen a drifter looking for work stumbles upon a pair of sun
 glasses that reveal the ruling class as a colonizing alien race\, he sets 
 out to expose and destroy the invaders. Roddy Piper and Keith David star a
 s down-on-their-luck\, working class men who discover that these undercove
 r aliens are broadcasting subliminal messages\, encouraging conformity and
  consumerism in a plot to rule Earth. Unabashed in its social and politica
 l commentary\, They Live reflects John Carpenter’s distaste for Reagan-e
 ra politics and commercialism. Based on Ray Nelson’s short story “Eigh
 t O’Clock in the Morning” and scored by Carpenter\, the film has devel
 oped a strong cult following and continues to find new fans with messaging
  that still resonates in our current political climate.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/they-live-with-john-c
 arpenter-019fc8bd-7eb2-9037-e9c7-c5ede38fe138
END:VEVENT
