SUMMARY:River of No Return
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260928T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260928T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc896-414a-51ec-2ce7-fc2577e83ef5@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, September 28\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy M
 useum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 31m\n\n1954 | 91 min | USA | Techn
 icolor | Scope | English | Not Rated | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Otto Preminger 
 \nPRODUCED BY: Stanley Rubin \nWRITTEN BY: Frank Fenton \nWITH: Robert Mit
 chum\, Marilyn Monroe\, Rory Calhoun\, Tommy Rettig\n\nType: Screenings\n
 \nMarilyn Monroe’s appearance in Western genre films required designer T
 ravilla to create costumes ranging from saloon-style gowns to casual denim
  looks. Monroe wanted her character\, Kay—a kind-hearted saloon singer t
 orn between an ex-convict (Robert Mitchum) and her troubled fiancé (Rory 
 Calhoun)—to have a natural feel. Her acting coach\, Natasha Lytess\, and
  director Otto Preminger clashed over whether Monroe should use her typica
 l breathy voice\, with the studio backing Monroe’s decision to forgo it.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/river-of-no-return-01
 9fc896-414a-51ec-2ce7-fc2577e83ef5
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Assault on Precinct 13 with John Carpenter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260928T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260928T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc8be-a43f-3889-be9f-d1e3d95ec179@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, September 28\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy M
 useum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 31m\n\n1976 | 91 min | USA | Color
  | Scope | English | Rated R | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: John Carpenter \nPROD
 UCED BY: J. Stein Kaplan \nWRITTEN BY: John Carpenter \nWITH: Austin Stoke
 r\, Darwin Joston\, Laurie Zimmer\, Kim Richards\n\nType: Screenings\n\nJo
 hn Carpenter's Assault on Precinct 13 locks audiences inside a decommissio
 ned South Central Los Angeles police station while Street Thunder gang mem
 bers exact revenge against the LAPD. Lieutenant Ethan Bishop (Austin Stoke
 r) is in charge of three convicts\, a startled\, silent citizen\, and a st
 rong-willed secretary as the gang outside their doors wreaks mayhem. Carpe
 nter's direction leads with his own score of high-intensity synthesizer mu
 sic accompanying Bishop on his crusade to heroism.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/assault-on-precinct-1
 3-with-john-carpenter-019fc8be-a43f-3889-be9f-d1e3d95ec179
END:VEVENT
