SUMMARY:Apocalypse Now: The Final Cut
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260930T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fc8ac-74f2-14e8-a9ff-c4e36600841a@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: production manager Barrie Osbourne and James Mockos
 ki\, film archivist and restoration supervisor for American Zoetrope \nSel
 ected by the Production and Technology Branch\n\nWednesday\, September 30
 \, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRunti
 me: 3h 3m\n\n1979 | 183 min.| USA | Color | Scope | English | Rated R | 4K
  DCP \nDIRECTED/PRODUCED BY: Francis Ford Coppola \nWRITTEN BY: John Miliu
 s\, Francis Ford Coppola \nWITH: Marlon Brando\, Robert Duvall\, Martin Sh
 een\, Dennis Hopper\n\nType: Screenings\n\nFrancis Ford Coppola’s epic\,
  Vietnam-set reimagining of Joseph Conrad’s novella Heart of Darkness se
 nds Willard (Martin Sheen) on a desperate jungle mission to “terminate w
 ith extreme prejudice” the mysterious Col. Kurtz (Marlon Brando). The ma
 king of Apocalypse Now was a famously difficult but resulted in an unforge
 ttable film full of remarkable technical achievements. The film received e
 ight nominations\, including Best Picture\, Art Direction and Film Editing
 \, and won for Vittorio Storaro’s spectacular cinematography and the imm
 ersive soundscape created by Walter Murch\, Mark Berger\, Richard Beggs\, 
 and Nat Boxer.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/apocalypse-now-the-fi
 nal-cut-019fc8ac-74f2-14e8-a9ff-c4e36600841a
END:VEVENT
