SUMMARY:Pan's Labyrinth in 3D with Guillermo del Toro
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261001T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce49-46cc-5458-af8f-22bc6f739bf3@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:North American premiere of the 3D version \nIn person: writer/
 director Guillermo del Toro\n\nThursday\, October 1\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nL
 ocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 58m\n\n2006 | 11
 8 min | Mexico/Spain | Color | Spanish | Rated R | 3D DCP \nDIRECTED/WRITT
 EN BY: Guillermo del Toro \nPRODUCED BY: Álvaro Augustín\, Alfonso Cuar
 ón\, Guillermo del Toro\, Bertha Navarro\, Frida Torresblanco \nWITH: Iva
 na Baquero\, Sergi López\, Maribel Verdú\, Doug Jones\n\nType: Screening
 s\n\nOfelia (Ivana Baquero)\, a 10-year-old girl in Francoist Spain\, disc
 overs a magical underworld in one of writer-director Guillermo del Toro’
 s most richly imagined fantasies. When Ofelia is lured into a labyrinth hi
 dden in the forest\, a faun emerges to reveal she is a long-lost princess.
  To return to her mystical kingdom\, Ofelia must complete three magical ta
 sks. The film earned six Academy Award nominations\, including Foreign Lan
 guage Film\, and won for its stunning Art Direction\, Cinematography\, and
  Makeup\, with del Toro regular Doug Jones playing the Faun and the Pale M
 an. \nPan’s Labyrinth appears here in a brand-new restoration and in 3D.
  Del Toro\, who personally supervised every stage of the new restoration f
 rom the original 35mm negative\, introduces the film in person. \nSpecial 
 thanks to Cineverse.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/pans-labyrinth-in-3-d
 -with-guillermo-del-toro-019fce49-46cc-5458-af8f-22bc6f739bf3
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:River of No Return
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce1f-f5ff-1ff5-897d-5d21a8ae54f2@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, October 2\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 31m\n\n1954 | 91 min | USA | Technico
 lor | Scope | English | Not Rated | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Otto Preminger \nPR
 ODUCED BY: Stanley Rubin \nWRITTEN BY: Frank Fenton \nWITH: Robert Mitchum
 \, Marilyn Monroe\, Rory Calhoun\, Tommy Rettig\n\nType: Screenings\n\nMar
 ilyn Monroe’s appearance in Western genre films required designer Travil
 la to create costumes ranging from saloon-style gowns to casual denim look
 s. Monroe wanted her character\, Kay—a kind-hearted saloon singer torn b
 etween an ex-convict (Robert Mitchum) and her troubled fiancé (Rory Calho
 un)—to have a natural feel. Her acting coach\, Natasha Lytess\, and dire
 ctor Otto Preminger clashed over whether Monroe should use her typical bre
 athy voice\, with the studio backing Monroe’s decision to forgo it.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/river-of-no-return-01
 9fce1f-f5ff-1ff5-897d-5d21a8ae54f2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hunt for the Wilderpeople with Taika Waititi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261002T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce4c-afca-9541-d990-7183a7ce07ef@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:A tribute to Sam Neill \nIn person: director Taika Waititi\n\n
 Friday\, October 2\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion
  Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 41m\n\n2016 | 101 min | New Zealand | Color | Sco
 pe | English | Rated PG-13 | 4K DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Taika Waititi \n
 PRODUCED BY: Carthew Neal\, Leanne Saunders\, Taika Waititi\, Matt Noonan 
 \nWITH: Sam Neill\, Julian Dennison\, Rima Te Wiata\, Rachel House\n\nType
 : Screenings\n\nRicky Baker (Julian Dennison)\, a Māori foster teen with 
 a knack for getting into trouble\, is placed into the warm care of Bella F
 aulkner (Rima Te Wiata) and her stern\, indifferent husband\, Hec (Sam Nei
 ll). When an unexpected tragedy strikes\, Ricky runs away into the New Zea
 land bush\, obligating Hec to seek him out. Thanks to a set of comical mis
 haps and misconceptions\, the two become subjects of a manhunt\, forcing t
 hem to go on the run and brave the wilderness. Sam Neill’s portrayal of 
 Hec is one of the actor’s most cherished performances as he deftly evolv
 es from reluctant guardian to a quietly tender father figure for Dennison
 ’s rambunctiously endearing Ricky. Adapted from the 1986 novel Wild Pork
  and Watercress by Barry Crump\, Hunt for the Wilderpeople premiered at th
 e Sundance Film Festival to critical acclaim. The film also broke box offi
 ce records in New Zealand that year\, becoming the most successful film ma
 de locally—excluding international co-productions—an achievement the f
 ilm still holds today.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/hunt-for-the-wilderpe
 ople-with-taika-waititi-019fce4c-afca-9541-d990-7183a7ce07ef
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hocus Pocus
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T121500
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce43-4a3f-fae7-4e44-5e86f2020350@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, October 3\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 36m\n\n1993 | 96 min. | USA | Color |
  English | Rated PG | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Kenny Ortega \nPRODUCED BY: Dav
 id Kirschner\, Steven Haft \nWRITTEN BY: Mick Garris\, Neil Cuthbert \nS
 TORY BY: David Kirschner\, Mick Garris \nWITH: Bette Midler\, Sarah Jessi
 ca Parker\, Kathy Najimy\, Omri Katz\n\nType: Screenings\n\nOn All Hallows
 ’ Eve\, skeptical teen Max and little sister Dani are trick-or-treating 
 in their new town of Salem\, Massachusetts\, when they accidentally resurr
 ect the Sanderson Sisters\, three 17th-century witches who were executed a
 fter terrorizing the town. The kids must team with Max’s crush\, Allison
 \, and Binx\, a boy cursed by the sisters to live out eternity as a cat\, 
 to put an end to the witches’ reign of terror before the sisters can ste
 al their souls. A box office and critical failure upon release\, Hocus Poc
 us gained cult status through annual Halloween reruns on Disney Channel an
 d the iconic performances from Bette Midler\, Sarah Jessica Parker\, and K
 athy Najimy as the witches.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/hocus-pocus-019fce43-
 4a3f-fae7-4e44-5e86f2020350
END:VEVENT
