BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stalker
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261007T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261007T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce29-bd11-31bd-9f3e-486fb3077abb@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Selected by the Production Design Branch\n\nWednesday\, Octobe
 r 7\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRu
 ntime: 2h 41m\n\n1979 | 161 min | U.S.S.R. | Color | Russian | DCP \nDIREC
 TED BY: Andrei Tarkovsky \nWRITTEN BY: Arkady Strugatsky\, Boris Strugatsk
 y\, Andrei Tarkovsky \nWITH: Alisa Freindlich\, Alekander Kaidanovsky\, An
 atoly Solonitsyn\, Nikolai Grinko\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThree men search 
 a dangerous\, restricted area known as the Zone looking for a secret room 
 that supposedly grants wishes. Director Andrei Tarkovsky (Solaris\, 1972) 
 faced unusual hardships during production\, including a literally toxic lo
 cation and problems with film stock that forced nearly an entire film’s 
 worth of reshoots. But the result—one of Tarkovsky's boldest and most ch
 allenging projects—has been cited as an influential work by directors an
 d production designers\, with its stark and evocative imagery credited to 
 Tarkovsky himself as art director\, working with Aleksandr Boym and set de
 corator Rashit Safiullin.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/stalker-019fce29-bd11
 -31bd-9f3e-486fb3077abb
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Big Trouble in Little China
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fcdac-482d-7d90-7fe4-d84bcfe95fe6@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, October 8\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mu
 seum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 40m\n\n1986 | 100 min | USA | Color
  | Scope | English | Rated PG-13 | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: John Carpenter \nP
 RODUCED BY: Larry J. Franco \nWRITTEN BY: Gary Goldman\, David Z. Weinste
 in\, W.D. Richter \nWITH: Kurt Russell\, Kim Cattrall\, Dennis Dun\, Jame
 s Hong\n\nType: Screenings\n\nJohn Carpenter’s San Francisco-set\, super
 natural spin on Hollywood’s Chinatown tropes populates the storied neigh
 borhood with mystical beings. Kurt Russell is antihero Jack Burton\, an ou
 tsider who’s clueless without his Chinese American friend Wang Chi (Denn
 is Dun). Teaming up to save Wang’s fiancé from the vicious Lords of Dea
 th\, the pair embarks on a curiously supernatural adventure through the st
 reet of this historic Bay Area district. Originally written as a period We
 stern\, this cult favorite is an off-kilter\, distinctly Carpenterian take
  on traditional action films\, buoyed with the filmmaker’s signature wry
  comedy. —Adapted from a note written by Arthur Dong.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/big-trouble-in-little
 -china-019fcdac-482d-7d90-7fe4-d84bcfe95fe6
END:VEVENT
