DESCRIPTION:Friday\, October 9\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 57m\n\n1954 | 117 min | USA | Color |
  English | Not Rated | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Walter Lang \nPRODUCED BY: Sol 
 C. Siegel \nWRITTEN BY: Phoebe Ephron\, Henry Ephron \nWITH: Ethel Merman
 \, Donald O'Connor\, Marilyn Monroe\, Dan Dailey\n\nType: Screenings\n\nTh
 e Donahue clan\, led by husband and wife Molly and Terry (Ethel Merman and
  Dan Dailey)\, navigate the ups and downs of show biz\, from their beginni
 ngs in Vaudeville to the Great Depression\, in this musical comedy with so
 ngs by Irving Berlin. The family’s close bond is further tested with the
  arrival of the talented and driven Vicky Parker (Marilyn Monroe). Costume
  designer Travilla played an integral role in shaping Marilyn Monroe’s p
 ublic image on- and off-screen. Together they famously produced looks that
  evaded censorship while still courting controversy. His designs for her s
 howgirl characters are of particular note.
