BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Fog in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fcdae-e077-355c-8056-cd70e34aefc8@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, October 9\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Muse
 um of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 29m\n\n1980 | 89 min | USA | Color | 
 Scope | English | Rated R | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: John Carpenter \nPRODUCE
 D BY: Debra Hill \nWRITTEN BY: John Carpenter\, Debra Hill \nWITH: Adrienn
 e Barbeau\, Jamie Lee Curtis\, Janet Leigh\, John Houseman\n\nType: Screen
 ings\n\nIn the small coastal California town of Antonio Bay\, an old local
  is spinning tales of a ghostly fog to children on the beach\, evoking ter
 rors from 100 years earlier. As the clock strikes midnight\, the fog and i
 ts vengeful spirits return\, once again wreaking havoc. The Fog is seen as
  a welcome return to the horror genre for Carpenter after the monumental s
 uccess of Halloween (1978). John Carpenter directs Jamie Lee Curtis\, Adri
 enne Barbeau\, and John Houseman through the haunting of Antonio Bay.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-fog-019fcdae-e077
 -355c-8056-cd70e34aefc8
