BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Little Vampire in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T121500
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce43-b9a7-6acf-46c8-25fdba2cb0c4@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, October 10\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 35m\n\n2000 | 95 min. | Netherlands
 \, Germany\, USA\, UK | Color | English | Rated PG | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: 
 Uli Edel \nPRODUCED BY: Richard Claus \nWRITTEN BY: Karey Kirkpatrick\, 
 Larry Wilson \nWITH: Jonathan Lipnicki\, Richard E. Grant\, Jim Carter\, 
 Alice Krige \nPrint courtesy of the Academy Film Archive\n\nType: Screeni
 ngs\n\nFriendless\, plagued by nightmares\, Tony Thompson\, 8\, struggles 
 to adapt to his new home in Scotland and reconcile his obsession with vamp
 ires. His nightmares seem to come true when he meets child vampire Rudolph
 \, though the two boys quickly become friends when they realize Tony’s n
 ightmares contain essential information for Rudolph to break a centuries-o
 ld curse. Based on Angela Sommer-Bodenburg's children’s book series of t
 he same name\, this charming and whimsical tale of finding friendship in u
 nlikely places is populated with eerie cemeteries\, beautifully designed a
 ristocratic costumes\, and\, of course\, vampire cows.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-little-vampire-01
 9fce43-b9a7-6acf-46c8-25fdba2cb0c4
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Get on the Bus 30th Anniversary Screening in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T180000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce7d-e21b-f9de-ccf8-cfa1d672c55b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Reuben Cannon\, Bill Borden\, Reggie Bythewood\, As
 hley Dean\, Hill Harper\, and Olden Lee\n\nSaturday\, October 10\, 2026 at
  3 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 2m\n\n
 1996 | 122 min. | USA | Color | English | Rated R | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: 
 Spike Lee \nPRODUCED BY: Reuben Cannon\, Barry Rosenbush\, Bill Borden \nW
 RITTEN BY: Reggie Rock Bythewood \nWITH: Ossie Davis\, Andre Braugher\, Ha
 rry Lennix\, Isaiah Washington\n\nType: Screenings\n\nIn October 1995\, gr
 oup of African American men board a bus for a cross-country trip to Washin
 gton D.C. They have different backgrounds and hold varying beliefs\, but t
 hey’re all on the way to the same march. Among them are a father and a t
 eenage son forced together by court order\; a gay couple on the verge of a
  breakup\; an aspiring actor who’s homophobic and loud about it\; and a 
 man whose father\, a police officer\, was killed\, he says\, “by a broth
 er.” Most of the film takes place in or around the moving bus as the con
 versations grow more personal\, and emotions roil to the surface. \nSpike 
 Lee’s Get on the Bus\, which was shot in three weeks\, was financed by a
  small group of men including Danny Glover\, Wesley Snipes\, Will Smith\, 
 and Johnnie Cochran. Inspired by the Million Man March of 1995\, Lee's fil
 m delves into the racism that has influenced Black communities for generat
 ions\, creating space for genuine\, and difficult\, discourse about the co
 mmunity’s inner and outward-facing conflicts.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/30th-anniversary-of-g
 et-on-the-bus-019fce7d-e21b-f9de-ccf8-cfa1d672c55b
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aliens in 70mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce46-5898-ade3-4872-08b52c0324a2@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, October 11\, 2026 at 2 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 17m\n\n1986 | 137 min. | USA/UK | Color
  | English | Rated R | 70mm \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: James Cameron \nSTORY B
 Y: James Cameron\, David Giler\, Walter Hill \nPRODUCED BY: Gale Anne Hurd
  \nWITH: Sigourney Weaver\, Michael Biehn\, Paul Reiser\, Lance Henriksen
 \nPrint provided by The Walt Disney Company.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nEllen 
 Ripley\, the only survivor of the commercial spaceship Nostromo\, is awake
 ned from a half-century of suspended animation only to find herself return
 ing to the last place she ever wanted to go— the planet where she first 
 encountered the alien that slaughtered her crewmates. Writer-director Jame
 s Cameron’s action-packed continuation of Ridley Scott’s 1979 sci-fi h
 orror classic won Oscars for its sound effects editing and visual effects 
 and received nominations for its film editing\, sound\, James Horner’s t
 ense score\, and Sigourney Weaver’s steely yet vulnerable performance as
  Ripley. The art direction of production designer Peter Lamont and set dec
 orator Crispian Sallis also garnered a nomination\, making a seamless visu
 al connection with the original film while creating a variety of imaginati
 ve yet utterly convincing new designs.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/aliens-019fce46-5898-
 ade3-4872-08b52c0324a2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Prince of Darkness in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fcdb0-0fc6-c6cb-200b-a4956125c273@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, October 11\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 42m\n\n1987 | 102 min | USA | Color 
 | Scope | English | Rated R \nDIRECTED BY: John Carpenter \nPRODUCED BY: L
 arry J. Franco\nWRITTEN BY: John Carpenter  \nWITH: Donald Pleasence\, Lis
 a Blount\, Victor Wong\, Jameson Parker\n\nType: Screenings\n\nQuantum phy
 sics Professor Howard Birack (Victor Wong) tasks his students with their m
 ost unusual assignment yet when a Catholic priest (Donald Pleasence) uncov
 ers a strange and ancient substance in a monastery. As the young scientist
 s investigate\, dark entities descend upon the church\, bringing represent
 atives of Satan to the Earthly plane. John Carpenter wrote\, directed\, an
 d co-scored Prince of Darkness as the second chapter in his Apocalypse Tri
 logy\, which begins with The Thing (1982)\, and finishes with In the Mouth
  of Madness (1995).
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/prince-of-darkness-01
 9fcdb0-0fc6-c6cb-200b-a4956125c273
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Seven Year Itch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce23-41b9-6b5f-6f14-ff1a281254c8@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, October 19\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 45m\n\n1955 | 105 min | USA | Color 
 | Scope | English | Not Rated | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Billy Wilder \nPRODUCED
  BY: Charles K. Feldman\, Billy Wilder \nWRITTEN BY: Billy Wilder\, George
  Axelrod \nWITH: Marilyn Monroe\, Tommy Ewell\, Evelyn Keyes\, Sonny Tufts
 \n\nType: Screenings\n\nOne of Monroe’s most successful roles was as The
  Girl in director Billy Wilder’s The Seven Year Itch\, a comedy about a 
 restless husband left to his own devices for the summer. To market the fil
 m\, photographer Sam Shaw proposed the indelible subway grate moment\, whi
 ch dozens of publicity photographers attended on location in New York City
 . Due to sound issues\, the real scene was shot on the 20th Century-Fox lo
 t in Los Angeles. Outside of this iconic scene\, the exhibition Marilyn Mo
 nroe: Hollywood Icon also features silk pajamas worn during a pivotal mome
 nt in developing Monroe’s girl-next-door character.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-seven-year-itch-0
 19fce23-41b9-6b5f-6f14-ff1a281254c8
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In the Mouth of Madness in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fcdb6-5fab-378b-4f89-99a1fa5dba6e@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, October 19\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 35m\n\n1995 | 95 min | USA | Color |
  Scope | English | Rated R | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: John Carpenter \nPRODUC
 ED BY: Sandy King \nWRITTEN BY: Michael De Luca \nWITH: Sam Neill\, Julie 
 Carmen\, Jürgen Prochnow\, Charlton Heston\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDirecte
 d and scored by John Carpenter\, and written by Michael De Luca\, this lov
 e letter to the work of H. P. Lovecraft sees insurance investigator John T
 rent (Sam Neill) journey to a mysterious small town\, unaware that he is e
 ntering the depths of insanity. Taking its name from Lovecraft’s 1936 no
 vella At the Mountains of Madness\, the final film in the Apocalypse Trilo
 gy follows Trent as he tracks down horror novelist Sutter Cane (Jürgen Pr
 ochnow)\, who has gone missing after completing his latest book. Word spre
 ads that anyone who reads an advance copy of the novel becomes a homicidal
  maniac\, but Trent is convinced it is all a publicity stunt—until his i
 nvestigation leads him to an eerie town identical to Cane’s work.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/in-the-mouth-of-madne
 ss-019fcdb6-5fab-378b-4f89-99a1fa5dba6e
END:VEVENT
