BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening of Short Films by Women Directors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce2d-087e-1067-868a-6806c769079d@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Selected by the Short Films Branch \nFree for museum members\n
 \nWednesday\, October 21\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of 
 Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 11m\n\nSmall Deaths \n1996 | 11 min. | UK | Co
 lor | English \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Lynne Ramsay \nPRODUCED BY: James De 
 Paor \nWITH: Anne McLean\, James Ramsay\, Lynne Ramsay Jr.\, Genna Gillan 
 \nSuicide by Sunlight \n2019 | 17 min. | USA | Color | English \nDIRECTED 
 BY: Nikyatu Jusu \nWRITTEN BY: Nikyatu Jusu\, Robin Shanea Williams \nPROD
 UCED BY: Nikkia Moulterie \nWITH: Natalie Paul\, Motell Gyn Foster\, Alexi
 s Nichole Smith\, Souleymane Sy Savane\nSome Boys Don't Leave\n2009 | 17 m
 in. | USA | Color | English\nDIRECTED BY: Maggie Kiley\nWRITTEN BY: Maggie
  Kiley\, Matthew Mullen\nPRODUCED BY: Jason Potash\nWITH: Jesse Eisenberg
 \, Eloise Mumford\, Jennifer Rau\, Keith Stone\nMabel’s Busy Day \n1914 
 | 12 min. | USA | Black-and-white | Silent \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Mabel No
 rmand \nPRODUCED BY: Mack Sennett \nWITH: Mabel Normand\, Charles Chaplin 
 \nLa Montaña \n2008 | 9 min. | Chile | Color | Spanish \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN
  BY: Dominga Sotomayor \nWITH: Gaspar Garrós\, Martin Villanueva \nGraceL
 and \n2020 | 14 min. | USA | Color | English \nDIRECTED BY: Bonnie Kathlee
 n Ryan \nWRITTEN BY: Bonnie Kathleen Ryan\, Trevor Munson \nPRODUCED BY: B
 onnie Kathleen Ryan\, Brad Jayne\, Stephen Moffatt\, Trevor Munson\, Kevin
  Peterson\, Ed Tilden \nWITH: Anna Camp\, Monique Coleman\, Daniel Eric Go
 ld\, Katie Beth West \nYo también \n2017 | 16 min. | Spain | Color | Span
 ish \nDIRECTED BY: Sonia Sebastián \nWRITTEN BY: Guillem Clua \nWITH: Mag
 gie Civantos\, María Hervás\, Jaume Ulled\, Eul à lia Ramón\n\nType: S
 creenings\n\nLynne Ramsay (We Need to Talk About Kevin\, 2011) directed Sm
 all Deaths (1996)\, an evocative look at key events in a girl’s life. Ni
 kyatu Jusu’s Suicide by Sunlight (2019) tells of Black vampires in a nea
 r-future New York. In Maggie Kiley's Some Boys Don't Leave\, a "Boy" is fo
 rced to come to terms with the fact that a "Girl" no longer wants him arou
 nd. The problem is\, he can't seem to leave their once-shared apartment. 
 \nSilent comedy star Mabel Normand directs herself and Charles Chaplin in 
 Mabel’s Busy Day (1914). Two estranged friends are reunited for a diffic
 ult journey in Dominga Sotomayor Castillo’s La Montaña (2008). A mom (A
 nna Camp) must cope with her daughter’s claim to be the reincarnation of
  Elvis Presley in Bonnie Kathleen Ryan’s comedy short GraceLand (2020). 
 In Sonia Sebastián’s Yo también (2017)\, a young woman has to inform h
 er romantic partners about her hepatitis diagnosis.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/an-evening-of-short-f
 ilms-by-women-directors-019fce2d-087e-1067-868a-6806c769079d
END:VEVENT
