BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vampires in 4K with Memoirs of an Invisible Man in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261023T213000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fcdd2-04c0-3ce5-734d-cf58b1fb1d61@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, October 23\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 47m\n\n1998 | 107 min | USA | Color 
 | Scope | English | Rated R \nDIRECTED BY: John Carpenter \nPRODUCED BY: S
 andy King \nWRITTEN BY: Don Jakoby \nWITH: James Woods\, Daniel Baldwin\, 
 Sheryl Lee\, Thomas Ian Griffith\n\nType: Screenings\n\nVampires in 4KBase
 d on John Steakley’s novel of the same name\, John Carpenter’s Vampire
 s is the master of horror’s sole foray into the realm of vampirism. The 
 film may be full of style and tropes influenced by classic Westerns\, incl
 uding a setting in New Mexico\, but the heroes brandish wooden stakes and 
 crossbows instead of rifles and six-shooters. Jack Crow (James Woods) lead
 s a team of grizzled\, Vatican-sponsored vampire hunters who seek to exter
 minate Valek (Thomas Ian Griffith)\, the first vampire\, now on a quest to
  gain immunity from the sun. Balancing action and one-liners with scares a
 nd gore\, all set to a Carpenter score\, Vampires is a fresh\, contemporar
 y take on the classic monsters of Universal and Hammer horror fame.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/vampires-with-memoirs
 -of-an-invisible-man-019fcdd2-04c0-3ce5-734d-cf58b1fb1d61
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monster Mash
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019f1fdb-7bb1-0d3a-96fc-ec6cc22ce4f2@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Calling all creatures of the night: join the Academy Museum fo
 r a fang-tastic day exploring the vampire\, the most famous creature of th
 e dark\, with special-effects demos\, thrilling tours\, monster appearance
 s\, and more.\n\nSaturday\, October 24\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academ
 y Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 30m\n\nAt a glance\n11am | Movi
 e | Hotel Transylvania (2012) | Ted Mann Theater\n11am–1:30pm | Special 
 effects makeup and hair demo | Grand Lobby  \n12:30–2:30pm | Vampire blo
 od SFX family workshop | Shirley Temple Education Studio | Lower Level 1\n
 1–5pm | Monster meet and greet | Grand Lobby  \n1:30\, 2:30\, and 3:30pm
  | The Horror Tours | Level 4\n2:30pm | Movie | Blade (1998) | Ted Mann Th
 eater \n4–5pm | Killer Fitness performance and dance-along | Grand Lobby
     \n7:30pm | Movie | Horror of Dracula (1958) | Ted Mann Theater\n\nType
 : Screenings\n\nCalling all creatures of the night: join the Academy Museu
 m for a fang-tastic day of special-effects makeup demonstrations\, thrilli
 ng tours\, monster appearances\, movies\, and activities—all exploring t
 he vampire\, the famous creature of the dark. Embrace this year’s theme 
 with Dracula\, vampire hunters\, and a relaxing monster resort.  \nFree wi
 th the purchase of a general admission ticket. Museum admission is free fo
 r youth 17 and under. \nDetails\n11am | Movie | Hotel Transylvania (2012) 
 | Ted Mann Theater | Lower Level 2\n11am–1:30pm | Special effects makeup
  and hair demo | Grand Lobby  \nA scary-good time with transformations by 
 special effects makeup artist Joel Harlow and Academy Award winner Howard 
 Berger.\nGeneral admission ticket not required. Program may end early.  \n
 12:30–2:30pm | Vampire blood special effects family workshop | Shirley T
 emple Education Studio | Lower Level 1\nGet mixed up in the world of horro
 r makeup with a lesson on creating Hollywood-worthy vampire blood\, featur
 ing tools used by real artists. All ages are welcome.\n1–5pm | Monster m
 eet and greet | Grand Lobby  \nMeet Universal Studios' classic movie monst
 ers—Dracula\, the Bride of Frankenstein\, and Frankenstein's monster—f
 or a can't-miss photo opportunity. It’ll be a scream.  \nGeneral admissi
 on ticket not required. Monsters meet for 30 minutes at a time.   \n1:30\,
  2:30\, and 3:30pm | The Horror Tours | Level 4\nOpen the door and peek in
 side—if you dare—with a museum educator on a 30-minute guide tour of T
 he Horror Show exhibition. Get a behind-the-scenes look at the representat
 ion of vampires and gothic horror in film\, and explore the production pro
 cesses for many horror classics.\nTours are limited to 25 people and are f
 irst-come\, first-served. Please arrive at the meeting place on Level 4 up
  to 10 minutes before the start time to secure your spot. General admissio
 n ticket required.   \nThis exhibition explores themes that may not be sui
 table for all ages and may disturb some visitors. Parental guidance is adv
 ised. If you have questions about the content\, please speak with a galler
 y associate. \n2:30pm | Movie | Blade (1998) | Ted Mann Theater | Lower Le
 vel 2\n4–5pm | Killer Fitness performance and dance-along | Grand Lobby 
    \nA horror performance and dance-along\, where fitness meets fear. \n7:
 30pm | Movie | Horror of Dracula (1958) | Ted Mann Theater | Lower Level 2
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/monster-mash-019f1fdb
 -7bb1-0d3a-96fc-ec6cc22ce4f2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hotel Transylvania
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T123000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce81-5d86-638d-b7d7-5394af35897e@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, October 24\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 31m\n\n2012 | 91 min. | USA | Color 
 | English | Rated PG | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Genndy Tartakovsky \nPRODUCED BY
 : Michelle Murdocca \nWRITTEN BY: Peter Baynham\, Robert Smigel \nSTORY BY
 : Todd Durham\, Dan Hageman\, Kevin Hageman \nWITH: Adam Sandler\, Andy Sa
 mberg\, Selena Gomez\, Kevin James\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA hapless young 
 backpacker (voiced by Andy Samberg) stumbles upon an Eastern European reso
 rt and falls for the owner’s daughter (Selena Gomez)\, unaware that he
 ’s discovered a hotel for monsters and that his prospective father-in-la
 w is Dracula himself. Adam Sandler leads the stellar comedic voice cast as
  the Count\, with Kevin James as Frankenstein’s monster\, Fran Drescher 
 as his bride\, Steve Buscemi as a werewolf\, and David Spade as the Invisi
 ble Man. Director Genndy Tartakovsky’s inventive visuals are an ideal ma
 tch for the script’s winning mixture of humor and sentiment. The film wo
 uld spawn three sequels and a TV series.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/hotel-transylvania-01
 9fce81-5d86-638d-b7d7-5394af35897e
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Blade in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T163000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce83-6b84-bb23-0a9e-f1f7b8d009b8@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, October 24\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy M
 useum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h\n\n1998 | 120 min | USA | Color | 
 Scope | English/Russian/Serbian | Rated R | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Stephen 
 Norrington \nPRODUCED BY: Peter Frankfurt\, Wesley Snipes\, Robert Engelma
 n \nWRITTEN BY: David S. Goyer \nWITH: Wesley Snipes\, Stephen Dorff\, Kri
 s Kristofferson\, N'Bushe Wright\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA vampire hunter k
 nown as Blade (Wesley Snipes) uses his superhuman abilities to protect hum
 anity from neck-biting undead under the guidance of mentor Abraham Whistle
 r (Kris Kristofferson). The half-undead\, half-human daywalker also seeks 
 revenge for his mother’s murder at the hands of a vampire during her pre
 gnancy. Based on the comic book series of the same name\, Blade was the fi
 rst film produced by Marvel Studios. An unexpected box-office success\, th
 e film helped pave the way for the Marvel Cinematic Universe. Snipes’s u
 ndeniable charisma as the leather-clad slayer and his decades of training 
 in martial arts helped cement the character’s place in pop culture.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/blade-019fce83-6b84-b
 b23-0a9e-f1f7b8d009b8
