BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Arrival: A Conversation with Denis Villeneuve and Dr. Nina Beguš
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261102T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261102T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019ff719-cda6-18c3-2355-e69ab8eb784c@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Conversations,Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: director Denis Villeneuve and Dr. Nina Beguš\n\nMo
 nday\, November 2\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 56m\n\n2016 | 116 min. | USA | Color | Scope | Eng
 lish | Rated PG-13 | DCP\nDIRECTED BY: Denis Villeneuve\nWRITTEN BY: Eric 
 Heisserer\nWITH: Amy Adams\, Jeremy Renner\, Forest Whitaker\, Michael Stu
 hlbarg\n\nType: Conversations\, Screenings\n\nInspired by Denis Villeneuve
 's 2016 sci-fi drama Arrival\, the director joins artificial-humanities sc
 holar Dr. Nina Beguš live in the David Geffen Theater for an inspiring co
 nversation about how language acts as a technology\; how fiction shapes ar
 tificial intelligence\; and how encounters with non-human intelligence mig
 ht transform our most basic understanding of thinking\, learning\, conscio
 usness\, time\, and more.  \nTo mark the 10th anniversary of this thought-
 provoking film\, an 8pm screening follows the discussion.\nAbout Nina Begu
 š Nina Beguš is a scholar and author working on AI\, literature\, and fi
 lm. She is a researcher at the University of California\, Berkeley\, where
  she leads the Artificial Humanities research group. Her work examines how
  stories\, concepts\, and cultural archetypes shape technology. She is the
  author of Artificial Humanities: A Fictional Perspective on Language in A
 I and the editor of First Encounters with AI: Writers on Writing. Beguš h
 olds a PhD in comparative literature from Harvard University and edits the
  Artificial Humanities book series at the University of Exeter Press. \nAb
 out Denis VilleneuveDenis Villeneuve is an Academy Award-nominated directo
 r\, screenwriter and producer whose masterful world-building and unique vi
 suals have established him as one of the premier filmmakers working today.
  \n\nIn 2021\, Dune: Part One earned six Academy Awards and multiple guild
  and critics' awards. Its sequel\, Dune: Part Two (2024)\, expanded with b
 older visual ambition and complexity\, surpassing $700 million worldwide a
 nd winning two Academy Awards\, with additional recognition from BAFTA\, C
 ritics Choice and major guilds. \n\nVilleneuve will conclude the trilogy w
 ith Dune: Part Three this December\, reuniting its core cast. He is also s
 et to direct the next James Bond film for Amazon MGM Studios. \nAbout the 
 film In director Denis Villeneuve’s thoughtful science-fiction drama\, a
 dapted from Ted Chiang’s award-winning novella Story of Your Life\, a li
 nguistics expert (Amy Adams) is recruited by the government when massive a
 lien spaceships suddenly land across the globe. The film’s production de
 signer\, Patrice Vermette (nominated with set decorator Paul Hotte) also d
 esigned the film’s alien language—one of Arrival’s many remarkable a
 nd imaginative visuals. The film was nominated in seven categories\, inclu
 ding Best Picture and Production Design\; it won an Oscar for Sound Editin
 g.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/arrival-a-conversatio
 n-with-denis-villeneuve-and-dr-nina-begus-019ff719-cda6-18c3-2355-e69ab8eb
 784c
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Last Princess (덕혜옹주)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261102T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261102T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce87-f9d1-0202-9756-8f2e3a175c8f@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, November 2\, 2026 at 8 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 7m\n\n2016 | 127 min | South Korea | Co
 lor | Scope | Korean/Japanese | Not Rated | DCP\nDIRECTED BY: Hur Jin-ho 
 \nWRITTEN BY: Hur Jin-ho\, Lee Han-eol\, Seo Yoo-min \nPRODUCED BY: Kim S
 ung-yong\, Shin Hye-yeun\, Park Hyun-tae \nWITH: Park Hae-il\, Son Ye-jin
 \, Ra Mi-ran\, Jung Sang-hoon\n\nType: Screenings\n\nIn the early 20th cen
 tury\, the last princess of the Korean royal family under Japanese rule is
  forced to move to Japan to attend school\, leaving behind her family\, fr
 iends\, and the only home she has ever known. Kim Jang-han (Park Hae-il)\,
  a childhood friend and Japanese army officer\, helps to plan an escape ro
 ute for her. This film\, based on the real story of Princess Deokhye (Son 
 Ye-jin)\, weaves fact with fiction to retell the story of a once-lost prin
 cess who stopped at nothing to return to the home she yearned for. –note
  written by Hannah Farkas.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-last-princess-019
 fce87-f9d1-0202-9756-8f2e3a175c8f
END:VEVENT
