SUMMARY:My Dad Is 100 Years Old with Rome\, Open City presented by Isabell
 a Rossellini
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T213000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce8c-8328-1ce4-64d2-ca0302f3fadb@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Isabella Rossellini\n\nWednesday\, November 4\, 202
 6 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 17
 m\n\n2005 | 17 min | Canada | Black-and-white | English | Not rated | DCP 
  \nDIRECTED BY: Guy Maddin  \nPRODUCED BY: Jody Shapiro  \nWRITTEN BY: 
 Isabella Rossellini  \nWITH: Isabella Rossellini\, Isaac Paz Sr.\n\nType:
  Screenings\n\nMy Dad Is 100 Years Old This short tribute casts celebrated
  actress Isabella Rossellini as herself as well as various filmmakers who 
 influenced or were influenced by her father\, filmmaker Roberto Rossellini
 . Conceived by Isabella on the eve of her father’s centenary\, she took 
 a “docu-fantasia” concept to avant-garde filmmaker Guy Maddin after he
 r delightful experience on his 2003 feature\, The Saddest Music in the Wor
 ld. A beautiful cinema poem for a beloved father and artist.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/my-dad-is-100-years-o
 ld-with-rome-open-city-019fce8c-8328-1ce4-64d2-ca0302f3fadb
