SUMMARY:Memories of Murder (살인의 추억) in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T210000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce98-88b8-c32d-e44b-c505ede880cb@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, November 4\, 2026 at 8 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 11m\n\n2003 | 131 min | South Korea 
 | Color | Korean | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Bong Joon Ho \nWRITTEN BY: Bong J
 oon Ho\, Shim Sung-bo \nPRODUCED BY: Kim Moo-ryoung\, Noh Jong-yoon\, Seun
 g-Jae Cha \nWITH: Song Kang-ho\, Kim Sang-kyung\, Byun Hee-bong\, Park Hae
 -il\n\nType: Screenings\n\nBong Joon Ho’s phenomenal breakthrough film s
 tars Park Hae-il as an enigmatic young loner and observer whose innocent d
 emeanor seems too wholesome to be true. Inspired by a true story\, Memorie
 s of Murder centers around the gruesome serial killings of women in South 
 Korea in the 1980s\, investigated by Doo-man (Song Kang-ho)\, a detective 
 who relies on instinct rather than fact. Bong’s vision\, which challenge
 s conventional components of storytelling and blurs the boundaries between
  genres\, is meticulously orchestrated in this crime thriller\, and Park
 ’s elegantly simple depiction of a complicated character is phenomenal.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/memories-of-murder-01
 9fce98-88b8-c32d-e44b-c505ede880cb
END:VEVENT
