SUMMARY:The Haunted Mansion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T121500
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce9c-5db0-34c6-1956-cdcf167842e5@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, November 7\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 28m\n\n2003 | 88 min. | USA | Color 
 | Scope | English | Rated PG | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Rob Minkoff \nPRODUCED
  BY: Don Hahn\, Andrew Gunn \nWRITTEN BY: David Berenbaum \nWITH: Eddie 
 Murphy\, Terence Stamp\, Nathaniel Parker\, Marsha Thomason\n\nType: Scree
 nings\n\nBased on the iconic Disneyland ride\, The Haunted Mansion stars E
 ddie Murphy as real estate agent Jim Evers\, a workaholic who wants to clo
 se a mansion deal before going on a much-needed vacation with his wife\, S
 ara\, and his kids. Upon their arrival\, the family is lured apart by ghos
 ts who believe Sara can set them free by joining them in the afterlife. Th
 e Evers family battles ghosts\, zombies\, and spiders to save Sara from et
 ernal damnation\, also encountering – of course -- references to the amu
 sement park ride\, including Hidden Mickeys and the theme song\, “Grim G
 rinning Ghosts.”
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-haunted-mansion-0
 19fce9c-5db0-34c6-1956-cdcf167842e5
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rossellini Through His Own Eyes (Rossellini visto da Rossellini)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce9d-9e8e-1db2-660d-0c4d5016dd79@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, November 7\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy M
 useum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 2m\n\n1993 | 62 min | Italy | Colo
 r\, Black-and-white | Italian\, French | Not Rated | DCP  \nDIRECTED BY: 
 Adriano Aprà \nWITH: Roberto Rossellini\, Ingrid Bergman\, Anna Magnani
 \, Isabella Rossellini\n\nType: Screenings\n\n“Neo-realism is above all 
 a moral standpoint from which to look at the world\,” Roberto Rossellini
  proclaimed in 1954\, and this conviction led him not just to make lasting
  contributions to the neo-realist mode\, but also equipped him to articula
 te his artistic ideas into spoken language. In this loving documentary por
 trait of the father of the cinematic movement\, scholar Adriano Aprà uses
  archival footage and interviews with Rossellini to underscore the filmmak
 er’s unique eloquence\, and the ways his life and work combined into his
  singular vision.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/rossellini-through-hi
 s-own-eyes-019fce9d-9e8e-1db2-660d-0c4d5016dd79
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rome\, Open City (Roma città aperta) in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fce9e-c52e-1ee3-a07b-2484acf4e5f2@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, November 7\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy M
 useum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 43m\n\n1945 | 103 min | Italy | Bl
 ack-and-white | Italian\, German\, Latin with English subtitles | Not rate
 d | 35mm\nDIRECTED BY: Roberto Rossellini  \nWRITTEN BY: Sergio Amidei\, 
 Federico Fellini\,  \nWITH: Aldo Fabrizi\, Anna Magnani\, Marcello Paglie
 ro\, Vito Annichiarico\n\nType: Screenings\n\nMade for less than $20\,000 
 just after the liberation of Italy by US forces\, Rossellini’s first ins
 tallment in his Neo-Realist Trilogy\, which also includes Paisan (1946\, s
 creening on November 15) and Germany\, Year Zero (1948\, screening the sam
 e day)\, is also considered the first product of neo-realism. The devastat
 ion of Nazi-occupied Rome serves as an all-too-real backdrop for a story t
 hat could have been ripped from the headlines: a resistance leader (Aldo F
 abrizi) is pursued through town as he seeks shelter and a safe escape. Wit
 h “the terror of German occupation [...] still vivid in the minds of eve
 ryone\,” (Patrizio Rossi\, 1988) including Rossellini’s lead actress\,
  the great Anna Magnani\, Rome\, Open City serves as a prototype for a ser
 ies of films that characterize the best of Italian cinema.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/rome-open-city-019fce
 9e-c52e-1ee3-a07b-2484acf4e5f2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chicago in 35mm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fcea0-a79c-07fd-95cf-01f9e0b0b58b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, November 8\, 2026 at 2 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum
  of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 53m\n\n2002 | 113 min. | USA/Canada | C
 olor | English | Rated PG-13 | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Rob Marshall \nWRITTEN 
 BY: Bill Condon \nPRODUCED BY: Martin Richards \nWITH: Renée Zellweger\, 
 Catherine Zeta-Jones\, Richard Gere\, Queen Latifah\nPrint courtesy of the
  Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nWannabe celeb Roxie Hart mur
 ders her lover and is sent to jail\, only to discover that a tabloid scand
 al may be her best route to true stardom in this stylish and lively versio
 n of the stage musical. Rob Marshall\, making his feature directing debut
 \, pays due homage to the distinctive style of Bob Fosse’s original Broa
 dway production while bringing his own energetic approach to the material
 \, which features such classic Kander and Ebb songs as “All That Jazz\,
 ” “Cell Block Tango\,” and “Mister Cellophane.” The first movie 
 musical to win Best Picture in the 34 years since Oliver! (1968)\, it rece
 ived 13 nominations and also won for Costume Design\, Film Editing\, Sound
 \, Catherine Zeta-Jones’s commanding performance as Roxie’s frenemy Ve
 lma Kelly. Production designer John Myhre and set decorator Gordon Sim als
 o won for their Art Direction\, featuring just the right blend of fantasy 
 and reality.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/chicago-019fcea0-a79c
 -07fd-95cf-01f9e0b0b58b
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Waikiki Brothers (와이키키 브라더스)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T213000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fceaa-0d8c-29c6-78fd-3da5a274eff0@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, November 8\, 2026 at 6:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 49m\n\n2001 | 109 min | South Korea 
 | Color | Korean | DCP \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Yim Soon-rye \nPRODUCED BY: 
 Lee Eun\, Shim Jae-myeong \nWITH: Lee Eol\, Hwang Jung-min\, Park Won-sang
 \, Park Hae-il\n\nType: Screenings\n\nPark Hae-il’s big-screen debut is 
 Yim Soon-rye’s second feature\, which received critical praise upon its 
 2001 release\, establishing Yim as one of Korea’s most significant direc
 tors. Seong-woo\, lead singer and guitarist of Waikiki Brothers—a band f
 ormed with his friends back in high school—returns to his hometown with 
 his bandmates in hopes of repairing their fragile relationship. But the ba
 nd stagnates\, and Seong-woo is torn between a dream that’s out of reach
  and his thin grasp on reality. Park\, who portrays the teen version of Se
 ong-woo\, generates youthful energy\, evoking the purity that Seong-woo an
 d his bandmates once carried and now long for. Yim’s insightful and huma
 ne perception of the cruel split between dreams and reality in modern Kore
 a permeates this portrayal of her sympathetic and intricate characters.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/waikiki-brothers-019f
 ceaa-0d8c-29c6-78fd-3da5a274eff0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Some Like It Hot in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fcea2-e597-ea37-537e-ba990f989094@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, November 9\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 1m\n\n1959 | 121 min | USA | Black-a
 nd-White | English | Not Rated | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Billy Wilder \nPROD
 UCED BY: Billy Wilder \nWRITTEN BY: Billy Wilder\, I. A. L. Diamond \nWITH
 : Marilyn Monroe\, Tony Curtis\, Jack Lemmon\, George Raft\n\nType: Screen
 ings\n\nMarilyn Monroe’s work in director Billy Wilder’s comedic class
 ic is often cited as her best. The film was controversial for its racy hum
 or and story about two musicians (Tony Curtis and Jack Lemmon) who disguis
 e themselves as women to evade the Mafia. But of equal scandal were the Os
 car-winning costumes made by Orry-Kelly for Monroe’s Sugar Kane Kowalczy
 k. Both dresses are on display in the exhibit Marilyn Monroe: Hollywood Ic
 on\, on view through February 28\, 2027. Some Like It Hot was made during 
 a year of dramatic highs and lows for Monroe\, with this film standing as 
 a high point.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/some-like-it-hot-019f
 cea2-e597-ea37-537e-ba990f989094
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moss (이끼)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261109T210000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fcea5-0914-56f5-74e2-969a3339a5ec@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, November 9\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mus
 eum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 43m\n\n2010 | 163 min | South Korea 
 | Korean\, Japanese | Not Rated  \nDIRECTED BY: Kang Woo-suk \nWRITTEN B
 Y: Jung Ji-woo \nPRODUCED BY: Jung Sun-young \nWITH: Park Hae-il\, Jeong
  Jae-yeong\, Yoo Joon-sang\, Yoo Seon\n\nType: Screenings\n\nHae-guk (Park
  Hae-il) receives word that his estranged father has passed away\, bringin
 g him to an unusual village for the funeral. Sensing his presence is unwel
 come\, Hae-guk grows suspicious and begins to sense a deeper truth behind 
 his father's death. Adapted from a Korean webtoon\, Moss submerges audienc
 es in a dark and thrilling mystery\, blending suspense and horror to creat
 e a world of uncertainty. –Note written by Hannah Farkas.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/moss-019fcea5-0914-56
 f5-74e2-969a3339a5ec
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Some Like It Hot in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fcea3-63d6-402d-d4df-8d5f6eceed43@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, November 11\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy
  Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 1m\n\n1959 | 121 min | USA | Bla
 ck-and-White | English | Not Rated | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Billy Wilder \n
 PRODUCED BY: Billy Wilder \nWRITTEN BY: Billy Wilder\, I. A. L. Diamond \n
 WITH: Marilyn Monroe\, Tony Curtis\, Jack Lemmon\, George Raft\n\nType: Sc
 reenings\n\nMarilyn Monroe’s work in director Billy Wilder’s comedic c
 lassic is often cited as her best. The film was controversial for its racy
  humor and story about two musicians (Tony Curtis and Jack Lemmon) who dis
 guise themselves as women to evade the Mafia. But of equal scandal were th
 e Oscar-winning costumes made by Orry-Kelly for Monroe’s Sugar Kane Kowa
 lczyk. Both dresses are on display in the exhibit Marilyn Monroe: Hollywoo
 d Icon\, on view through February 28\, 2027. Some Like It Hot was made dur
 ing a year of dramatic highs and lows for Monroe\, with this film standing
  as a high point.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/some-like-it-hot-019f
 cea3-63d6-402d-d4df-8d5f6eceed43
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:War for the Planet of the Apes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261111T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fcea6-3bd2-a751-b0ce-f79d4ffa1e83@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Selected by the Visual Effects Branch\n\nWednesday\, November 
 11\, 2026 at 7:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRun
 time: 2h 20m\n\n2017 | 140 min. | USA | Color | Scope | English | Rated PG
 -13 | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Matt Reeves \nPRODUCED BY: Peter Chernin\, Dylan
  Clark\, Rick Jaffa\, Amanda Silver \nWRITTEN BY: Mark Bomback\, Matt Reev
 es \nWITH: Andy Serkis\, Woody Harrelson\, Steve Zahn\, Karin Konoval\n\nT
 ype: Screenings\n\nThe third film in the contemporary version of the Plane
 t of the Apes series finds the ape leader Caesar (another remarkable motio
 n capture performance by Andy Serkis) seeking a safe haven for the survivo
 rs of a human-led massacre\, only to wind up in a labor camp run by a vici
 ous military officer (Woody Harrelson). The film was nominated for the vis
 ual effects by Joe Letteri\, Daniel Barrett\, Dan Lemmon and Joel Whist\, 
 who depict the film’s ape characters and wintry\, post-apocalyptic setti
 ng with astonishing realism.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/war-for-the-planet-of
 -the-apes-019fcea6-3bd2-a751-b0ce-f79d4ffa1e83
END:VEVENT
