SUMMARY:The Misfits in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T160000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fceb2-2191-b9ef-b1b8-e8bd741c5187@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, November 20\, 2026 at 2:30 pm\n\nLocation: Academy Mu
 seum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 5m\n\n1961 | 125 min | USA | Black-
 and-White | English | Not Rated | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: John Huston \nPROD
 UCED BY: Frank E. Taylor \nWRITTEN BY: Arthur Miller \nWITH: Clark Gable\,
  Marilyn Monroe\, Montgomery Clift\, Thelma Ritter\nRestored by the Academ
 y Film Archive and The Film Foundation. Restoration funding provided by th
 e Hobson/Lucas Family Foundation.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nPenned by Arthur 
 Miller\, this contemporary Western centers on the recently divorced Roslyn
  (Marilyn Monroe) and her relationship with an aging former cowboy\, Gay (
 Clark Gable)\, who now survives by rounding up wild mustangs to sell them 
 to a slaughterhouse. Considered a commercial failure at the time of its or
 iginal release\, the film has since been regarded as a classic by critics 
 and audiences\, perhaps notably because it was the final completed film of
  both Gable and Monroe\, and a fitting bookend to Monroe’s career—she 
 credited Huston for her first big break in his The Asphalt Jungle (1950).
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-misfits-019fceb2-
 2191-b9ef-b1b8-e8bd741c5187
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Journey to Italy (Viaggio in Italia) in 4K
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T223000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fceb5-ef5d-bf8f-6798-bb9bfde1aafd@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:US restoration premiere\n\nFriday\, November 20\, 2026 at 7:30
  pm\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 25m\n\n1
 954 | 85 min | Italy/France | Black-and-white | English/Italian with Engli
 sh subtitles | Not Rated | 4K DCP\nDIRECTED/PRODUCED BY: Roberto Rossellin
 i  \nWRITTEN BY: Vitaliano Brancati\, Roberto Rossellini  \nWITH: Ingrid
  Bergman\, George Sanders\, Maria Mauban\, Anna Proclemer\n\nType: Screeni
 ngs\n\nUS restoration premiere\n“It was very important for me to show It
 aly\, Naples\,” Rossellini said in 1954\, “that strange atmosphere so 
 imbued with a very real\, very immediate\, very deep feeling: the sense of
  eternal life.” The fantastic Ingrid Bergman and George Sanders play Kat
 herine and Alex Joyce\, an unhappily married English couple of eight years
  whose trip to Italy takes them along separate\, and possibly permanently 
 diverging\, paths. Bergman’s fourth film with then-husband Roberto Rosse
 llini allows her to relax into a natural acting style that would become a 
 blueprint for 1960s actors and filmmakers interested in presenting fresh\,
  grounded performances.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/journey-to-italy-019f
 ceb5-ef5d-bf8f-6798-bb9bfde1aafd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wendell & Wild
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T123000
DTSTAMP:20260902T123625Z
UID:019fceb6-94fe-1960-94f0-62fd5b1b66a0@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, November 21\, 2026 at 11 am\n\nLocation: Academy Mu
 seum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 45m\n\n2022 | 105 min. | USA\, Irel
 and\, Bulgaria\, Canada | Color | English | Rated PG-13 | DCP \nDIRECTED 
 BY: Henry Selick \nPRODUCED BY: Henry Selick\, Ellen Goldsmith-Vein\, Jor
 dan Peele\, Win Rosenfeld\nWRITTEN BY: Henry Selick\, Jordan Peele \nWITH
 : Jordan Peele\, Keegan-Michael Key\, Angela Bassett\, Lyric Ross\n\nType:
  Screenings\n\nThe director of Coraline (2009) and The Nightmare Before Ch
 ristmas (1993) brings his eerie whimsy to a macabre tale of an orphaned pu
 nk\, Kat. Haunted by her parents' death and disappointed with other adults
 \, she is shuttled off to a failing boarding school\, where she discovers 
 her ability to summon demons. Two of them\, voiced by Keegan-Michael Key a
 nd Jordan Peele\, manipulate Kat into bringing them to the land of the liv
 ing with a promise of resurrecting her parents\, but bringing people back 
 from the dead never turns out quite as planned. With spectacular stop-moti
 on animation\, an inspired Afro-punk soundtrack\, and kooky antics aplenty
 \, this is a charming take on the importance of community\, standing up fo
 r what's right\, and befriending your demons.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/wendell-wild-019fceb6
 -94fe-1960-94f0-62fd5b1b66a0
END:VEVENT
